====================================================================================================
PART 0 - SANITY GATE (inherited from haste_economics.py).  At fee=0 the competitive
  arb's profit per block must equal the textbook LVR rate sigma_b^2 * V / 8.
====================================================================================================
  calm      ~40% ann: theory=$  0.0152/blk  simulated=$  0.0152/blk  err=  0.2%  PASS
  normal    ~60% ann: theory=$  0.0342/blk  simulated=$  0.0341/blk  err=  0.4%  PASS
  stressed ~120% ann: theory=$  0.1370/blk  simulated=$  0.1376/blk  err=  0.4%  PASS
  longtail ~300% ann: theory=$  0.8562/blk  simulated=$  0.8544/blk  err=  0.2%  PASS

  Flow calibration: median retail notional $5,000 in a $40M constant-product pool
  => median tick impact 5.0 ticks.  LP fee 5 bps.  3 retail swaps/block.
    calm      ~40% ann: sigma_block =  2.47 ticks  (retail impact / block vol =  2.03x)
    normal    ~60% ann: sigma_block =  3.70 ticks  (retail impact / block vol =  1.35x)
    stressed ~120% ann: sigma_block =  7.40 ticks  (retail impact / block vol =  0.68x)
    longtail ~300% ann: sigma_block = 18.51 ticks  (retail impact / block vol =  0.27x)
  Column key: 'hon bps' = volume-weighted SWITCHBACK bps paid by honest flow;
  'arb-cau' = share of that fee whose retracement consumed extension created by the
  corrective ARB rather than by other flow (LIFO attribution).  This is the H1 channel.
  'sw esc' = % of baseline-profitable in-block sandwiches still profitable;
  'arb kill' = % of profitable corrective arbs we deter outright; 'arb short' = mean
  fraction of the full correction left undone.

======================================================================================================================
PART 1 - MANDATORY NEGATIVE CONTROLS.  If these misbehave the RIG is wrong, not SWITCHBACK.
======================================================================================================================
  NC1  no staleness, ONE-WAY honest flow  -> charged 0.00% , 0.0000 bps   PASS (must be exactly 0)
  NC2  no staleness, ALTERNATING honest flow -> charged 51.15% , 2.36 bps   PASS (meter can fire)
       This is 2.4f and it is NOT a staleness effect: intra-block two-sided honest
       flow pays even with a perfect reference.
  NC3  fee OFF (gamma=0), full flow -> charged 0.00% , sandwich escape 100.0% , 25% of victims attackable   PASS
  NC4  STALENESS FLOOR: market frozen, arb ON, fee OFF -> block-open staleness 4.32 ticks
       PASS (pool sits inside the no-arb band, so the rig CAN keep a fresh reference)
  NC5  SAME WORLD, FEE ON (gamma=1) -> staleness 11.37 ticks (2.63x the floor), arb killed 0.0% , correction shortfall 29.7%
       NOT a control - this is the OZ warning reproduced with ZERO exogenous
       volatility.  The staleness above the floor is caused BY SWITCHBACK.

  ALL CONTROLS PASS.

======================================================================================================================
PART 2 - THE CHEAP ANSWER FIRST.  Does the intra-block extension cap already bound it?
  Staleness cannot enter the fee formula directly - the fee is a pure function of the
  intra-block path relative to T0, and T0 IS the pool's own price at block open, so it
  is never stale relative to the thing the fee measures.  Staleness can only act by
  changing FLOW.  These three worlds isolate that.
======================================================================================================================
scenario                          staleT0  hon chg  hon bps  arb-cau  sw esc  sw keep arb kill arb short  fee$/blk
(a) frozen mkt, no arb            275.26t    34.1%    2.54b     0.0%   30.8%     1.9%     0.0%      0.0%      7.72
(b) mkt moves, NO arb (max stale)  290.77t    34.6%    2.73b     0.0%   31.7%     1.7%     0.0%      0.0%      8.11
(c) mkt moves, arb ON (realistic)   11.56t    44.6%    3.79b    38.0%   24.6%     1.6%     0.0%     26.3%     15.43
(d) as (c) + PERFECT reference*    15.77t    48.6%    4.39b     0.0%   21.3%     1.4%     0.0%     67.5%     22.06
  * (d) replaces T0 with the true market tick.  Not implementable on-chain.  NOTE: an
    earlier draft of this row left the extension budget empty at block open while
    moving T0, so the standing displacement was not chargeable, and it reported that a
    perfect reference HELPED.  With the budget seeded consistently it does the
    opposite: anchoring to the true market taxes price discovery itself (arb shortfall
    jumps to ~68%).  The intrinsic-vs-reference split is the 'arb-cau' column and NC2,
    not this row.
  (a)->(b): pure staleness with no corrective arb.  If SWITCHBACK were reference-
            sensitive in the OZ sense, honest cost would explode here.
  (b)->(c): adds the corrective arb, whose FREE extension is hypothesis H1.

