PART 10 - REFERENCE CARRY.  Can T0 survive a block boundary without a new exemption?
  EMA policy: T0_new = T0_old + alpha*(tick_at_block_open - T0_old).
  alpha=1 is the shipped hook (T0 resets fully); alpha=0 is a fixed anchor that never
  moves.  The budget is seeded with the standing displacement at block open so the M2'
  identity still holds; at alpha=1 that seed is exactly 0, which is why the alpha=1 row
  reproduces every earlier number bit-for-bit (NEGATIVE CONTROL).
  'IN' = in-block sandwich, 'XB' = the PART 8 cross-block unwind, re-scored per policy.
